## Rework after the review (F1 blocker, F2 minor)

**F1 (responsive layout).** The first version switched layouts at `max-width: 520px`, which was
above the real toolbar wrap (the toolbar needs 427 px, so it wraps only below ~451 px of surface
width) and far below the width where the toolbar stops touching card A's home (~832 px of surface
width) and the zone stops touching card B (~740 px). Between 521 px and ~890 px the demo therefore
had two real overlaps.

The rework replaces the breakpoint pair with one consistent compact range:

- `@media (max-width: 900px)` (surface width up to 900 px) turns `.demo__surface` into a two-row grid
  (`grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); grid-template-rows: auto minmax(0, 1fr)`) and moves the
  toolbar into the first row (`position: static; justify-self: center; margin-block: var(--space-12)`).
  The row height follows the real toolbar height, so the single-row toolbar (54 px) and the wrapped
  two-row toolbar (94 px) both reserve exactly the right strip — no extra breakpoint and no magic
  offset. `.demo__world` becomes the second row (`position: relative; inset: auto`) and the surface
  grows to `--canvas-grid` × 54 (864 px) so the zone has vertical room between the two card homes.
- The desktop arrangement is kept unchanged from 901 px (surface 853 px and wider): the toolbar
  floats over the canvas at the top centre and the zone sits at the canvas centre.
- The zone keeps the already-working 390 px placement (absolute, centred in the world layer,
  `margin-block-start: var(--space-32)`); in the compact range the vertical gap to both card homes
  comes from the taller world, in the desktop range from the horizontal separation.
- `preview.js` measures the world layer instead of the surface for the card clamp and the edge
  `viewBox` (identical on desktop: world 1134 × 358 inside a 1136 × 360 surface border box).

**F2 (log sizes).** The first log quoted HTTP sizes captured before the final HTML edit
(`56115` for `index.html`). All HTTP sizes below were re-measured against the committed files and
match the byte sizes on disk.

## Port and server

Slot values (`python3 "$POLIER/tools/slot.py" show`, and `.polier-slot`): `web=4200` for slot 2. The
port is read from `.polier-slot`, never hard-coded. The server was started and stopped by this task
only; nothing else was started or stopped.

```sh
cd "/Users/rasulatashev/Desktop/KI Projekte/Project air-P0-26"
PORT=$(python3 -c "import json;print(json.load(open('.polier-slot'))['ports']['web'])")
python3 -m http.server "$PORT" --bind 127.0.0.1
```

Served the **repository root** so the relative token, icon and image paths resolve
(`../../../packages/ui-kit/...`, `assets/demo-zone-image.webp`).

