## Screenshots

Chrome for Testing:
`/Users/rasulatashev/Library/Caches/ms-playwright/chromium-1248/chrome-mac-arm64/Google Chrome for Testing.app/Contents/MacOS/Google Chrome for Testing`
(version 156.0.8078.4).

`--window-size=390,844` is clamped by Chrome to a wider window (Chrome's minimum window width), so
every viewport in this run was rendered through the Chrome DevTools Protocol with real device-metrics
emulation instead of a command-line window. A temporary, out-of-repo helper drove the protocol; it is
not part of the deliverable and was removed after the run.

```sh
CHROME="/Users/rasulatashev/Library/Caches/ms-playwright/chromium-1248/chrome-mac-arm64/Google Chrome for Testing.app/Contents/MacOS/Google Chrome for Testing"
"$CHROME" --headless=new --disable-gpu --hide-scrollbars \
  --remote-debugging-port=9333 --user-data-dir=/tmp/p026-chrome-profile about:blank &

cd "/Users/rasulatashev/Desktop/KI Projekte/Project air-P0-26"
node /tmp/p026-cdp2.mjs "http://127.0.0.1:4200/apps/web/preview/" "reviews/evidence"
```

The helper used only built-in Node APIs (`fetch` + the global `WebSocket`) and these CDP calls:

| Step | CDP call |
| --- | --- |
| enable | `Page.enable`, `Runtime.enable`, `DOM.enable`, `CSS.enable` |
| views | `Emulation.setDeviceMetricsOverride {width, height, deviceScaleFactor: 1, mobile: width < 500}` |
| load | `Page.navigate` to the URL above, wait for `Page.loadEventFired`, then 500 ms |
| capture | `Page.captureScreenshot {format: "png", fromSurface: true}` (base64 written to the file) |
| states | `DOM.getDocument` + `DOM.querySelector` + `CSS.forcePseudoState` with `["hover"]`, `["focus", "focus-visible"]` and `["active"]`, then 600 ms and the same capture call |
| mid width | 768 × 900 metrics, `window.scrollTo(0, surfaceTop + scrollY - 18)`, then the same capture call |

Result sizes (`sips -g pixelWidth -g pixelHeight`, `stat -f '%z'`):

- `reviews/evidence/P0-26-desktop.png` — PNG 1440 × 900, 164709 bytes (the desktop layout: the whole
