## Responsive width matrix (real layout measurements)

Every width was loaded fresh at a 900 px viewport (`mobile: true` below 500 px) and measured with
`getBoundingClientRect` plus the live card transforms. `World layer` is the layer the cards live on
(second grid row in the compact range, the whole surface on desktop); `Cards at home` compares the
live card transforms with the 4 %/5 % and 90 %/90 % home formula on that world layer.

| Viewport | Surface | Toolbar rows | World layer | Overlaps | Page h-overflow | Cards at home |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 390 | 358 × 864 | 2 | 356 × 744 | none | False | True / True |
| 400 | 368 × 864 | 2 | 366 × 744 | none | False | True / True |
| 430 | 398 × 864 | 2 | 396 × 744 | none | False | True / True |
| 450 | 418 × 864 | 2 | 416 × 744 | none | False | True / True |
| 480 | 448 × 864 | 1 | 446 × 784 | none | False | True / True |
| 500 | 468 × 864 | 1 | 466 × 784 | none | False | True / True |
| 520 | 488 × 864 | 1 | 486 × 784 | none | False | True / True |
| 521 | 489 × 864 | 1 | 487 × 784 | none | False | True / True |
| 600 | 568 × 864 | 1 | 566 × 784 | none | False | True / True |
| 700 | 668 × 864 | 1 | 666 × 784 | none | False | True / True |
| 768 | 720 × 864 | 1 | 718 × 784 | none | False | True / True |
| 860 | 812 × 864 | 1 | 810 × 784 | none | False | True / True |
| 900 | 852 × 864 | 1 | 850 × 784 | none | False | True / True |
| 901 | 853 × 360 | 1 | 851 × 358 | none | False | True / True |
| 1000 | 952 × 360 | 1 | 950 × 358 | none | False | True / True |
| 1200 | 1136 × 360 | 1 | 1134 × 358 | none | False | True / True |
| 1440 | 1136 × 360 | 1 | 1134 × 358 | none | False | True / True |

What the matrix proves:

- **Zero overlaps** between the toolbar and the zone, the toolbar and either card, the zone and either
  card, the zone and the zoom pill, each card and the zoom pill, and the two cards — at every width from
  390 px to 1440 px, including both sides of the layout switch (900 / 901 px) and the toolbar wrap
  boundary (450 / 480 px).
- **No horizontal page overflow** at any width (`scrollWidth == clientWidth == bodyScrollWidth`).
- **The cards keep their home positions** of the world layer: 4 %/5 % for card A and 90 %/90 % for
  card B, snapped to the 16 px canvas grid, at every width.
- **Layout switch:** compact (two-row grid, surface 864 px tall, world layer below the toolbar row)
  up to a 900 px viewport; desktop (360 px surface, toolbar floating over the canvas) from 901 px.
  The boundary rows show the reason for the switch: at 900 px the compact world is 850 × 784 and the
  toolbar sits in its own row; at 901 px the desktop surface is 853 × 360 and the toolbar (237…664)
  clears card A (57…233) by 4 px horizontally while the zone (314…588) clears card B (633…809).

